The wforce-common package provides /etc/wforce/regexes.yaml and creates the
wforce system account shared by wforce, trackalert and replfwd.

Daemon configuration templates are installed in /usr/share/wforce,
/usr/share/wforce-trackalert and /usr/share/wforce-replfwd. Their active
configuration files in /etc/wforce are managed by ucf, preserving local
changes across upgrades. Credentials are generated during configuration,
and the active files are readable only by their owner and group (wforce).
Purging a daemon package removes its configuration and ucf registration.
Purging wforce-common only removes empty shared directories, preserving
administrator-created files and backups.

The upstream wforce-lua-dist dependency and builder-provided libraries are
retained. Debian-specific source patches and release metadata are not part
of this packaging.
